- independent dependency-safe branches may run concurrently only inside admission/resource/fanout limits;
- use isolated clean worktrees under {str(consumer.get('worktree_root') or Path(consumer['workspace']) / 'worktrees').rstrip('/')}/ for code changes;
- never write directly to main, bypass CI/review/rulesets, widen child permissions, create unbounded retries/fallbacks/fanout, or fabricate acceptance evidence;
- merge only after required tests, exact-head green CI and independent exact-head review with no unresolved applicable finding;
- after every merge re-read live main/issues/PRs and replan immediately;
- keep root #{number} open until every agent-compatible Herdr issue is satisfied and any remainder is explicitly evidenced as a genuine gate.

Gate handling:
- a gated leaf must not stop the root while another dependency-ready AUTO issue is available;
- do not mark the root user_action_required merely because one leaf is gated;
- if only an elapsed-time ACCEPTANCE_GATE remains (for example the #9 >=24h clean soak), return a completed cycle with precise next_action so intake can re-check after cooldown; never manufacture elapsed time;
- use a blocking root result only when no safe AUTO work remains and progress truly requires human input, a new credential/secret, a paid/billing decision, an external dependency, sudo/production deployment or another irreversible privileged action.

Do not flatten the Herdr backlog into duplicate outer durable tasks. This root owns backlog selection and bounded delegation.
""".strip()

    if name == "quantlab":
